172
00:52:34,909 --> 00:52:46,857
按照常用记号，令 G_i 为i 的稳定子群（stabilizer）。记住这是 A_n，所以它自然作用在该集合上，我们当然可以令 G_i为稳定子群。
We'll let G_i be, as per the usual notation, the stabilizer of i.

173
00:52:52,440 --> 00:53:10,820
它同构于什么？G_i 长什么样？没错，它同构于 A_{n-1}！啊哈，而 A_{n-1} 由归纳假设是单群！
What is this isomorphic to? What does G_i look like? Exactly: it is A_{n-1}! Aha, well A_{n-1}, by induction hypothesis, is simple!

174
00:53:10,820 --> 00:53:17,435
因此这其中的核心要害，就是利用稳定子群是单群这一事实。
So the crux of this thing is going to be to leverage the fact that we know that the stabilizers are simple.

175
00:53:17,435 --> 00:53:21,640
单群性至关重要！
Simplicity is important!

176
00:53:25,250 --> 00:53:38,264
我将给出一系列断言，每个都不算特别难证，它们加在一起就能完成证明；但大家必须自己补全细节，因为我们时间不够了。
So I'm going to give you a series of claims, none of which are particularly difficult to show, and they will prove this; but you have to fill in the details for these claims because we are out of time.

177
00:53:38,264 --> 00:54:11,883
断言 1 是：在 H 中不存在元素——记住 H 是G 的反设非平凡真正规子群——在 H 中不存在非恒等元素 τ 能够固定某个 i。
First claim is that there does not exist an element of H—so remember H is this putative non-trivial proper normal subgroup of G—there does not exist tau in H other than the identity such that tau fixes some i.

178
00:54:11,883 --> 00:54:27,243
我的意思是，你最终使用这个性质的方式是——为了让这里的逻辑联系更清晰，更容易弄懂接下来的断言：如果我知道对某个 i 有 τ_1(i) = τ_2(i)（其中 τ_1, τ_2 ∈ H），
So I mean, the way that you end up using this—just to make the connection here clearer, to make it easier to figure out what happens in the next claims: if I know that tau_1(i) = tau_2(i),

179
00:54:27,243 --> 00:54:57,805
那么我就能知道实际上 τ_1 = τ_2；因为——我写成这样，这推导出——因为这样一来 τ_2^{-1} τ_1(i)等于 i，所以它固定 i，从而必须是恒等元，故 τ_1 必等于 τ_2。那么怎么证明这一点呢？
tau_1 and tau_2 being in H, then I know that in fact tau_1 = tau_2, since—I'll put it this way, this implies that—since then tau_2^{-1} tau_1(i) equals i, so this thing must be the identity, so tau_1 must equal tau_2. So how do you show this?

180
00:54:57,805 --> 00:55:41,548
简化版思路是：该证明需要证明对所有 j，稳定子群 G_j 必须是 H 的子群（G_j ⊆ H）；进而说明 A_n——它是由所有这些 G_j 生成的——是 H 的子群，从而 H 是整个 A_n（H = G），与H 是真子群的假设矛盾！
Well, the simplified version is to show: the proof of this involves showing that G_j must be a subgroup of H for all j, and then showing that A_n, which is generated by all of the G_j's, is a subgroup of H, and so H is all of A_n, H is all of G, contradicting the hypothesis that H is proper!

181
00:55:41,548 --> 00:56:25,052
所以真正的关键是证明每个 G_j 都是 H 的子群；这完全是在运用我们目前所学的方法。接下来的两件事如下：断言 2：在 H 中给定 τ，其不相交轮换分解中只能出现 2-轮换（对换）。
So that's a contradiction. So the real point is to show this fact that every G_j is a subgroup of H, and that's just using the sorts of things that we've done so far. And then the last two things are the following: so Claim 2: given tau in H, only 2-cycles can appear in its disjoint cycle decomposition.

182
00:56:28,028 --> 00:56:51,010
而断言 3 恰好相反：在 H 中给定 τ，τ 在其分解中不可能只含 2-轮换。
Then Claim 3 is the opposite: given tau in H, tau doesn't just have 2-cycles in its decomposition.

183
00:56:58,010 --> 00:57:08,276
证明这些断言的方法，就是取一个反设的元素（τ ∈ H），然后证明可以通过共轭得到另一个元素，
And the way you show these things is just by taking a putative element, and then showing that you have some other element you can get to by conjugating that,

184
00:57:08,276 --> 00:57:30,238
并证明这两个元素（该共轭元素与原元素）必然将某个特定元素映为相同的元素，必然将某个数字映为相同的数字，于是这就完成了！
showing that those two elements, the conjugate and the original element, must take a certain element to the same element, and must take a certain number to the same number, and then that's it.
